node_modules/
strikes.json
audit.log
*.tmp
config.yaml
# ...and its dated backups. config.yaml holds the appservice tokens, so a
# timestamped copy of it holds them too -- and an untracked file that must
# NEVER be committed still shows as drift on every sweep, which trains you to
# ignore the light. Ignored, not committed.
config.yaml.bak.*
tunnel-registration.yaml
# The pre-rename name. The file still exists on disk and still holds live
# tokens: renaming the ignore entry alone un-ignored it, and `git add -A`
# promptly staged it as a rename of the EXAMPLE file. Both names stay listed
# for as long as the old file exists.
bmb-registration.yaml
.env

# CLAUDE.md is canon for a PUBLIC repo, so it lives in fourier-basis
# (docs/claude/CLAUDE-fourier-tunnel.md) and is hydrated here as a local, ignored
# file. A public repo carrying one in-tree is a policy breach; this is the
# guard technetium has had since 2026-08-25 and chanbooru did not.
CLAUDE.md
